Before online shopping became popular, businesses used electronic systems to exchange information such as purchase orders, invoices and transaction records. One important technology was Electronic Data Interchange (EDI), which allowed businesses to exchange standardised documents electronically rather than relying on traditional paper-based communication.

These early systems established the foundations of modern e-commerce by making business transactions faster, more organised and less dependent on physical paperwork.


